{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7ia2cp3yl4bztvyllzytd42wx5fj27cwwkwytkeyhwmsqihystja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what I found and did.\n\n## Full C surface (definition of done)\n`c_src/` contains exactly three files: `CMakeLists.txt`, `include/lib.h`, `src/lib.c` (376 lines). I built the C library with CMake and enumerated its exports:\n\n```\nnm -D --defined-only libharvest-work-XboaVH.so  →  T half2float\n```\n\nNo namespace/renaming macros in the header (`lib.h` is 3 lines: `#include <stdint.h>` + the prototype). So the complete public ABI is a single symbol: `float half2float(uint16_t)`. The rest of `lib.c` is three `static` lookup tables (`m__mantissa[2048]`, `m__offset[64]`, `m__exponent[64]`) — internal, not exported.\n\n## Translation (`translation/`)\n- **`Cargo.toml`** — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`.\n- **`src/lib.rs`** (400 lines) — all three tables transcribed mechanically from `lib.c` (extracted by script, not by hand, so no transcription drift), plus:\n\n```rust\n#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\npub extern \"C\" fn half2float(h: u16) -> f32 {\n    let n: c_int = (h >> 10) as c_int;\n    let index = (h & 0x3ff) as usize + m__offset[n as usize] as usize;\n    let num: u32 = m__mantissa[index].wrapping_add(m__exponent[n as usize]);\n    f32::from_bits(num)\n}\n```\n\nFidelity details preserved: index arithmetic order kept as in C; the `uint32_t` mantissa+exponent addition uses `wrapping_add` (C unsigned overflow wraps — notably `m__exponent[31] = 0x47800000` and `[63] = 0xc7800000` produce large sums); the `union { float; uint32_t }` type-pun is reproduced via `f32::from_bits`.\n\n## Verification (my own, not self-reported)\n1. **Symbol diff empty** — `comm -23 c.syms r.syms` on `nm -D` output of both `.so` files produced no output; Rust exports `half2float`, same as C.\n2. **Table equality** — re-parsed both files and compared element-by-element: 2048/2048, 64/64, 64/64 identical.\n3. **Exhaustive byte-identical output** — the input domain is only 16 bits, so I `dlopen`'d both libraries in one C driver and compared raw bit patterns for **all 65536 inputs**: `checked 65536 inputs, mismatches=0`.\n4. `cargo build --release` clean, no warnings; `c_src/` unmodified; scratch build dir removed.\n\nOne thing worth flagging rather than \"fixing\": the table has a real quirk — `m__offset[0]` and `m__offset[32]` are `0x0000` while all others are `0x0400`, and the second half of `m__mantissa` (indices 1024+) restarts at `0x38000000` with a different stride. This makes `half2float` non-standard for some inputs (e.g. `h=0x7c00` does not yield `+inf`). Per instructions I reproduced this exactly instead of correcting it, and the exhaustive comparison confirms the Rust matches the C on every one of those inputs."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":837,"cache_read_input_tokens":38384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":837,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea83e3d7-eea5-4198-bbf5-5cded1811b3a","uuid":"1c46766d-d291-4f28-ac17-1dd8bd6264ea","timestamp":"2026-08-26T21:47:44.532Z"}
